      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "READY FOR AIMEE (2) fell a head shy from making it two on the bounce at Ipswich, with the winner saluting again in Saturday grade. Strips rock-hard fit and gets in well again at the weights with Pozman claiming 3kgs. PEARLS IN JUNE (7) returns off a six-week freshening after winning comfortably here last time when first-up. Boasts a strong record over this track and trip and is drawn favourably with more to offer. Big threat. TASMAN BAY (3) has returned in good order and finds another suitable contest, coming off a Doomben third after winning there. Sure to be competitive again. EXUBERANCE (5) is the value danger after a sound fourth in Saturday company here when wide throughout. Not underestimating.",
